<title>ITALY: Lira ERM re-entry level not Naples topic -- Prodi.</title>
<headline>Lira ERM re-entry level not Naples topic -- Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>NAPLES, Italy 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Romano Prodi did not expect the level at which Italy would re-enter the European Exchange Rate (ERM) mechanism to be a topic at the Italy-French summit in Naples.</p>
<p>&quot;The question of (the level of the re-entry of the lira in the ERM) will be discussed on the collective level. It is not a subject of bilateral talks,&quot; he told reporters in answer to a question.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a necessary and automatic step if one takes part in monetary union,&quot; he said of re-entry into the ERM.</p>
<p>The lira crashed out of the ERM in September 1992.</p>
<p>Prodi was speaking to reporters in Naples ahead of French President Jacques Chirac's arrival for a bilateral summit.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom - 39-6-678-2501</p>
